              "ev-4b7756ab59de-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 44,
              "start": 12
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Justices asked about various principles and hypothetical scenarios concerning pre\u2011trial delays, including whether a broader principle beyond calculating delay periods is relevant (Justice Alito), how the facts would change if the defendant never spoke on the record (Justice Souter), the role of public defenders and whether they work for the State (Chief Justice Roberts), and whether delays by State\u2011appointed counsel are always attributable to the State (Justice Kennedy)."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Christina Rainville",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "4b7756ab59de8d030fa5f55d7a49978787d94fe59d9a5b054441f13f20f6ecdb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-4b7756ab59de-0000-0001",
              "ev-4b7756ab59de-0000-0005",
              "ev-4b7756ab59de-0000-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 19,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioner counsel Christina Rainville argued that the delays were caused by non\u2011State actors, that the defendant had waived speedy\u2011trial rights, and that the Vermont Supreme Court\u2019s decision should be reversed."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "MS. KRUGER",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "4b7756ab59de8d030fa5f55d7a49978787d94fe59d9a5b054441f13f20f6ecdb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-4b7756ab59de-0001-0001",
              "ev-4b7756ab59de-0001-0003",
              "ev-4b7756ab59de-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to MS. KRUGER, amicus counsel Leondra R. Kruger contended that attributing delay to the State would undermine lawyers\u2019 discretion and emphasized the ethical duty of counsel to avoid unreasonable delays."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Oral Argument",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
