  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Christina Rainville",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "4b7756ab59de8d030fa5f55d7a49978787d94fe59d9a5b054441f13f20f6ecdb",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-4b7756ab59de-0000-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Christina Rainville, there are many reasons to reverse the Vermont Supreme Court in this case."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Christina Rainville",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "4b7756ab59de8d030fa5f55d7a49978787d94fe59d9a5b054441f13f20f6ecdb",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-4b7756ab59de-0000-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 18,
                "start": 18
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Christina Rainville, the delays in this case were caused by non\u2011State actors and, as a matter of law, cannot be a constitutional violation."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Christina Rainville",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "4b7756ab59de8d030fa5f55d7a49978787d94fe59d9a5b054441f13f20f6ecdb",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-4b7756ab59de-0000-0006"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 19,
                "start": 19
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Christina Rainville, based on his concessions and admissions in the brief, the defendant has waived the right to a speedy trial, applying the standard waiver doctrine from Barker v. Wingo."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner \u2013 Vermont (represented by Christina Rainville)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "MS. KRUGER",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "4b7756ab59de8d030fa5f55d7a49978787d94fe59d9a5b054441f13f20f6ecdb",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-4b7756ab59de-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 20,
                "start": 20
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to MS. KRUGER, a rule attributing delay to the State would be inconsistent with the role of a lawyer in an adversarial system and would undermine a lawyer's authority to make day\u2011to\u2011day scheduling decisions."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "MS. KRUGER",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "4b7756ab59de8d030fa5f55d7a49978787d94fe59d9a5b054441f13f20f6ecdb",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-4b7756ab59de-0001-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 22,
                "start": 22
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to MS. KRUGER, defendants can waive their right to a speedy trial and often desire to postpone trial; the remedy for a speedy\u2011trial violation uniquely advantages defendants and imposes substantial burdens on society, so a defendant cannot escape responsibility for continuances they requested."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "MS. KRUGER",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "4b7756ab59de8d030fa5f55d7a49978787d94fe59d9a5b054441f13f20f6ecdb",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-4b7756ab59de-0001-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 23,
                "start": 23
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to MS. KRUGER, the principal safeguard against attorney\u2011caused delay is the attorney's ethical obligation to represent clients with reasonable diligence and promptness."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Amicus Curiae \u2013 United States (represented by Leondra R. Kruger)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    }
